{{!--
  The rune circle, shared by the HUD and the GM control panel.

  Expects a rune-shaped context — `runes`, `seatCount`, `seatedCount`,
  `seatLabel`, `circleLabel` from `buildRuneView` — spread over the usual track
  fields, of which it reads `current`, `target`, `threshold` and `complete`.

  Each rune is an absolutely positioned span rather than an SVG node, the same
  way the ladder places its ticks: it keeps `data-tooltip` and text rendering
  working, and it lets one CSS transition carry a rune from its drift to its
  seat. Both positions are computed in JS (`runeSeats`), so there is no
  arithmetic here and the whole figure scales from the plate's own width.

  A rune's *state* is never colour alone: a seated rune is upright, bright and
  on the ring, while an unearned one is dim, tilted and outside it — and the
  centre readout spells the count out in digits regardless.

  A seat the GM has named carries a mark, the same promise the step strip makes
  about a labelled pip: which seats mean something is visible without hovering
  every one of them. A mark whose name the reader may not read yet is drawn
  hollow, so "there is something here" and "here is what it is" stay visibly
  different. The name of the seat the circle is standing on is printed under the
  plate, so the one that matters right now is readable outright.

  The plate is aria-hidden and the wrapper carries the full label, so a screen
  reader announces "Seal the Rift, 3 of 8 runes in place" rather than reading a
  loose alphabet.
--}}
<div class="pvc-runes{{#if complete}} pvc-runes-complete{{/if}}{{#if threshold}} pvc-tone-{{tone}}{{/if}}"
     role="img" aria-label="{{circleLabel}}" data-seats="{{seatCount}}">

  <div class="pvc-runes-plate" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="pvc-runes-glow"></span>
    <span class="pvc-runes-rim"></span>
    <span class="pvc-runes-ring"></span>

    {{#each runes}}
    <span class="pvc-rune{{#if seated}} pvc-rune-seated{{else}} pvc-rune-adrift{{/if}}{{#if active}} pvc-rune-active{{/if}}{{#if hidden}} pvc-rune-hidden{{/if}}{{#if tone}} pvc-tone-{{tone}}{{/if}}"
          style="left: {{left}}%; top: {{top}}%; --pvc-rune-tilt: {{rotation}}deg;"
          data-tooltip="{{tooltip}}">{{#if labelled}}<span class="pvc-rune-mark"></span>{{/if}}{{glyph}}</span>
    {{/each}}

    <span class="pvc-runes-core">
      <span class="pvc-runes-value">{{current}}</span>
      {{#unless threshold}}
      <span class="pvc-runes-divider">/</span>
      <span class="pvc-runes-target">{{target}}</span>
      {{/unless}}
    </span>
  </div>

  {{!-- The caption sits inside the `role="img"` wrapper, so it is decoration as
        far as a screen reader is concerned — `circleLabel` carries the same name
        for it. --}}
  {{#if seatLabel}}
  <span class="pvc-runes-caption">{{seatLabel}}</span>
  {{/if}}
</div>
